-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 1א', §1.9 נסיעות
-- Travel: the commuting allowance (with and without a free monthly pass, and
-- outside the employee's jurisdiction), organised transport in official
-- education, duty travel, and travel to further studies.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `1.9 נסיעות`

GIVEN d IS A DATE, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE d `is on or after` e IF
    DATE_SERIAL d AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL e

-- The actors §1.9 gives duties to that the takanon's shared Party list lacks.
@desc Actors of section 1.9 that are not in the takanon's shared Party list.
DECLARE `1.9 party` IS ONE OF
    `the district transport committee`
    `the personal-matters committee`
    `the head of the local education department`

DECLARE `committee action` IS ONE OF `decide the case`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9/p2 The page's table of contents (heading).
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9/p4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9/p6 Entries of the table of contents, naming the four subsections encoded below.

§§ `1.9.1 הוצאות נסיעה`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1/p1 A review note: the subsection was checked on 19.11.02.

@desc One month of a teaching employee's commuting, as far as section 1.9.1 asks about it.
DECLARE `commuting month` HAS
    `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `passes the journey needs`                IS A NUMBER  @desc 1, or 2 where the journey needs two passes
    `price of a monthly pass`                 IS A NUMBER  @desc an input
    `days employed a week`                    IS A NUMBER
    `real travel expenses of the month`       IS A NUMBER  @desc an input
    `needs transport to reach work`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `published allowance for a full month`    IS A NUMBER  @desc the allowance the Ministry's comptroller publishes from time to time (section 1.9.1.1ב.1); an input
    `published allowance per journey`         IS A NUMBER  @desc the same, per journey; an input
    `required to attend only some days`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc on a full or part-time position, required to come only on some of the week's days (1ב.3)
    `journeys made`                           IS A NUMBER
    `in a month after the first of a continuous paid absence longer than a month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc 1ב.5: from the start of the second month of such an absence
    `in a month after the first of reserve duty longer than a month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on unpaid leave`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `work temporarily stopped`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `a month of the summer break`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc one of the two summer-break months

§§§ `1.9.1.1א Where a free monthly pass operates`

-- 1א ¶4: one employed one or two days a week is paid real expenses "בכל
-- מקרה" — in any case, whatever else 1א or the clauses its note brings in
-- would pay.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_a/p4
GIVEN m IS A `commuting month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid real expenses in any case` m IF
    m's `days employed a week` AT MOST 2

-- F-1.9-e: 1ב.1 pays only one who needs transport to reach work; 1א
-- names no such condition and its note does not bring 1ב.1 in. Encoded as
-- printed: where a pass operates, the price of the pass, needed or not.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_a/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_a/p3
GIVEN m IS A `commuting month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `allowance where a pass operates` m IS
    IF `paid real expenses in any case` m
    THEN m's `real travel expenses of the month`
    ELSE m's `price of a monthly pass` TIMES min (m's `passes the journey needs`) 2

-- The note to 1א: "סעיפים 2(3), ב2(5) ו-ב2(6) להלן" apply to pass users too.
-- F-1.9-a: no clause of §1.9.1 bears those numbers; the reading adopted is
-- 1ב.3, 1ב.5 and 1ב.6 — journeys made, a long absence, and leave, stoppage
-- or summer.
-- "בכל מקרה" puts 1א ¶4 ahead of the per-journey rule (1ב.3): a teacher
-- employed one or two days a week attends on some days only, and is paid
-- her real expenses, not the published allowance per journey. The bars of
-- 1ב.5–6 still come first: a month they bar has no journey to pay for.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_a/p5
GIVEN m IS A `commuting month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pass user's allowance` m IS
    BRANCH IF `no allowance this month` m THEN 0
           IF `paid real expenses in any case` m
              THEN m's `real travel expenses of the month`
           IF m's `required to attend only some days`
              THEN m's `published allowance per journey` TIMES m's `journeys made`
           OTHERWISE `allowance where a pass operates` m

-- F-1.9-a's evidence: the clauses §1.9.1 numbers, and the three the note cites.
DECLARE `clause of 1.9.1` HAS
    `paragraph`  IS A NUMBER
    `letter`     IS A STRING
    `item`       IS A NUMBER  @desc 0 where the clause has no numbered items

`the clauses 1.9.1 numbers` MEANS
    LIST `clause of 1.9.1` 1 "א" 0,
         `clause of 1.9.1` 1 "ב" 1, `clause of 1.9.1` 1 "ב" 2, `clause of 1.9.1` 1 "ב" 3,
         `clause of 1.9.1` 1 "ב" 4, `clause of 1.9.1` 1 "ב" 5, `clause of 1.9.1` 1 "ב" 6,
         `clause of 1.9.1` 2 "א" 0, `clause of 1.9.1` 2 "ב" 0, `clause of 1.9.1` 2 "ג" 0,
         `clause of 1.9.1` 2 "ד" 1, `clause of 1.9.1` 2 "ד" 2, `clause of 1.9.1` 2 "ד" 3,
         `clause of 1.9.1` 2 "ה" 0

-- "2(3)" is paragraph 2, item 3; "ב2(5)" and "ב2(6)" are letter ב of
-- paragraph 2, items 5 and 6.
`the clauses the note cites` MEANS
    LIST `clause of 1.9.1` 2 "" 3, `clause of 1.9.1` 2 "ב" 5, `clause of 1.9.1` 2 "ב" 6

`the clauses the reading adopts` MEANS
    LIST `clause of 1.9.1` 1 "ב" 3, `clause of 1.9.1` 1 "ב" 5, `clause of 1.9.1` 1 "ב" 6

`none of the clauses the note cites exists` MEANS
    all (GIVEN c YIELD (NOT elem c `the clauses 1.9.1 numbers`)) `the clauses the note cites`
#ASSERT `none of the clauses the note cites exists`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD elem c `the clauses 1.9.1 numbers`) `the clauses the reading adopts`

§§§ `1.9.1.1ב Where no free monthly pass operates`

-- ב.1: the allowance, at the amount the comptroller publishes, for one who
-- needs transport; ב.3: by journeys made where attendance is required only
-- on some days.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_b akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_3
GIVEN m IS A `commuting month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `allowance without a pass` m IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT m's `needs transport to reach work`) THEN 0
           IF `no allowance this month` m THEN 0
           IF m's `required to attend only some days`
              THEN m's `published allowance per journey` TIMES m's `journeys made`
           OTHERWISE m's `published allowance for a full month`

-- ב.2: the second bus is paid for where it rides 3 urban stops or more,
-- not counting the stop of origin, and no shorter way can be walked.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2
GIVEN `buses needed` IS A NUMBER
      `urban stops on the second bus, not counting the first` IS A NUMBER
      `a shorter way can be walked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may claim for the second bus`
        `buses needed` `urban stops on the second bus, not counting the first` `a shorter way can be walked` IF
        `buses needed` GREATER THAN 1
    AND `urban stops on the second bus, not counting the first` AT LEAST 3
    AND (NOT `a shorter way can be walked`)

-- ב.4: in official education only, one employed in several schools is
-- attached to the one where the hours are greatest. F-1.9-b: a tie is not
-- decided; this returns every school with the greatest hours, so a tie
-- shows as more than one.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_4
GIVEN `hours in each school` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `schools the allowance attaches to` `hours in each school` IS
    filter (GIVEN h YIELD h EQUALS foldr max 0 `hours in each school`) `hours in each school`

`a teacher with 12 hours in each of two schools is attached to both` MEANS
    count (`schools the allowance attaches to` (LIST 12, 12)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `a teacher with 12 hours in each of two schools is attached to both`

§§§ `1.9.1.1ב.5–6 When no allowance is paid`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_5
GIVEN m IS A `commuting month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `barred by a long absence` m IF
        m's `in a month after the first of a continuous paid absence longer than a month`
    OR  m's `in a month after the first of reserve duty longer than a month`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_6 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_6__pnt_a akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_6__pnt_b akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_6__pnt_c
GIVEN m IS A `commuting month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `barred by leave, stoppage or summer` m IF
        m's `on unpaid leave`
    OR  m's `work temporarily stopped`
    OR  m's `a month of the summer break`

§§§ `1.9.1.1 The allowance, as 1א and 1ב compose`

-- 1ב.5 and 1ב.6 together, and the two cases of 1א and 1ב; shown beside none
-- of those paragraphs because each says only its part.
GIVEN m IS A `commuting month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no allowance this month` m IF
    `barred by a long absence` m OR `barred by leave, stoppage or summer` m

@export default The monthly commuting allowance a teaching employee is owed under section 1.9.1.1 of the takanon, with or without a free monthly pass
GIVEN m IS A `commuting month` @desc the employee's month
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `commuting allowance` m IS
    IF m's `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives`
    THEN `pass user's allowance` m
    ELSE `allowance without a pass` m

§§§ `1.9.1.2 Employed outside the jurisdiction of residence`

@desc A teaching employee who works outside the jurisdiction where she lives, as section 1.9.1.2 asks about it.
DECLARE `work outside the jurisdiction` HAS
    `posted there for the system's needs`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `moved home out of the jurisdiction`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the move raised the travel expenses or first made them payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc 2ב: the move increases the travel expenses, or makes the employee entitled to them from now on
    `moved at the Ministry's demand`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `moved for personal reasons the committee recognised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc health, marriage, children's education, bad housing and the like (2ב)
    `in official education`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `asked for a transfer and the Ministry agreed`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transfer took the workplace further from home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc 2ג: by the transfer the employee "התרחק ממקום מגוריו"
    `moved to another city and still works in the old one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `asked for work in the new city and was not placed for two years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a realistic placement in the new city was not used` IS A BOOLEAN
    `real bus fares for the days travelled`         IS A NUMBER
    `allowance before the move`                     IS A NUMBER
    `allowance at the previous workplace`           IS A NUMBER
    `allowance on the present journey`              IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_2__subpara_a
GIVEN w IS A `work outside the jurisdiction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid real bus fares as posted` w IF
    w's `posted there for the system's needs`

-- 2ב: a move out of the jurisdiction that raises the travel expenses, or
-- first makes them payable, keeps the allowance at its rate before the move,
-- unless it was at the Ministry's demand or for recognised reasons.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_2__subpara_b
GIVEN w IS A `work outside the jurisdiction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `frozen at the rate before the move under 2ב` w IF
        w's `moved home out of the jurisdiction`
    AND w's `the move raised the travel expenses or first made them payable`
    AND (NOT w's `moved at the Ministry's demand`)
    AND (NOT w's `moved for personal reasons the committee recognised`)

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_2__subpara_c
GIVEN w IS A `work outside the jurisdiction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `held at the previous workplace's rate under 2ג` w IF
        w's `in official education`
    AND w's `asked for a transfer and the Ministry agreed`
    AND w's `the transfer took the workplace further from home`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_2__subpara_d akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_2__subpara_d__cls_1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_2__subpara_d__cls_2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_2__subpara_d__cls_3
GIVEN w IS A `work outside the jurisdiction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid travel expenses under 2ד` w IF
        w's `in official education`
    AND w's `moved to another city and still works in the old one`
    AND w's `asked for work in the new city and was not placed for two years`
    AND w's `a realistic placement in the new city was not used`

-- 2ג ¶2: the personal-matters committee decides the cases of 2ב and any
-- case brought before it.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_2__subpara_c/p2
GIVEN `a case is brought under 2ב or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.9 party` `committee action`
DECIDE `the personal-matters committee decides` `a case is brought under 2ב or otherwise` IS
    IF `a case is brought under 2ב or otherwise`
    THEN PARTY `the personal-matters committee`
         MUST  `decide the case`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1__para_2__subpara_e A pointer: travel of northern teachers who teach in Bedouin localities in the south is in section 1.48.

§§§ `1.9.1.2 The allowance outside the jurisdiction, as 2א–2ד compose`

-- F-1.9-c: a teacher in official education who moved away meets 2ב (frozen
-- at the old rate) and, on 2ד's three conditions, 2ד (paid travel
-- expenses). The reading adopted: 2ד is the exception to 2ב and pays the
-- present journey. F-1.9-f: 2א and 2ב, 2ב and 2ג, and 2ג and 2ד also
-- reach one teacher with different rates, and the text orders none of
-- them; the order adopted is 2א, then 2ד, then 2ג, then 2ב.
@export The commuting allowance under section 1.9.1.2 of a teaching employee who works outside the jurisdiction where she lives
GIVEN w IS A `work outside the jurisdiction` @desc the employee's situation
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `allowance outside the jurisdiction` w IS
    BRANCH IF `paid real bus fares as posted` w THEN w's `real bus fares for the days travelled`
           IF `paid travel expenses under 2ד` w THEN w's `allowance on the present journey`
           IF `held at the previous workplace's rate under 2ג` w
              THEN min (w's `allowance on the present journey`) (w's `allowance at the previous workplace`)
           IF `frozen at the rate before the move under 2ב` w
              THEN min (w's `allowance on the present journey`) (w's `allowance before the move`)
           OTHERWISE w's `allowance on the present journey`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1/p4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1/p6 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_1/p7 The subsection's sources (אסמכתא): circulars and decisions of the parity committee.

§§ `1.9.2 הסעות מורים בחינוך הרשמי`

DECLARE `kind of official institution` IS ONE OF
    `a mixed kindergarten (ages 3–4 and compulsory)`
    `a compulsory kindergarten`
    `a primary school`
    `a middle school`
    `another institution`

@desc A proposed organised transport for teachers, as section 1.9.2.3–4 asks about it.
DECLARE `transport proposal` HAS
    `teachers need organised transport`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `public transport lines can be used`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved beforehand by the district transport committee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `can be combined with existing pupil transport`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `pupils walk the way`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `within the approved yearly budget`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `for parents' or staff meetings, home visits and the like` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the teachers receive the travel allowance`       IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `transport action` IS ONE OF
    `submit a request for the travel allowance to the district office's treasury`
    `decide on organised transport`
    `organise the transport and set a pick-up point`
    `weigh transport in placing teachers`
    `build the timetable for one pick-up and one drop-off`
    `submit a request for organised transport`
    `pass the request to the district committee`
    `approve organised transport`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_1
GIVEN k IS A `kind of official institution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transport rules of 1.9.2 apply in` k IF
    (NOT (k EQUALS `another institution`))

-- 2: those who need public transport get the allowance of 1.9.1; the
-- request goes to the treasury of the Ministry's district office.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_2
GIVEN `needs public transport between home and the institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the allowance of 1.9.1 under 1.9.2` `needs public transport between home and the institution` IF
    `needs public transport between home and the institution`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `transport action`
DECIDE `requesting the travel allowance under 1.9.2` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `submit a request for the travel allowance to the district office's treasury`

-- 3.1: no duty on the Ministry; where teachers need it and public transport
-- cannot be used, the Ministry MAY decide on organised transport.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_3__subpara_1
GIVEN p IS A `transport proposal`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `transport action`
DECIDE `the Ministry may organise transport` p IS
    IF p's `teachers need organised transport` AND (NOT p's `public transport lines can be used`)
    THEN PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MAY `decide on organised transport`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_3__subpara_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `transport action`
DECIDE `district managers weigh transport` IS
    PARTY `the district manager`
    MUST  `weigh transport in placing teachers`
    LEST BREACH BY `the district manager` BECAUSE "section 1.9.2.3: transport is weighed as a high-priority factor in placing teachers"

GIVEN `recommended by the district manager or his delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approved by the teaching manpower division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a placement is made as 1.9.2.3 asks`
        `recommended by the district manager or his delegate`
        `approved by the teaching manpower division` IF
    `recommended by the district manager or his delegate` AND `approved by the teaching manpower division`

-- 4: the rules for organised transport, as conditions on running it.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_7 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_8 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_9
GIVEN p IS A `transport proposal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `organised transport may run` p IF
        p's `approved beforehand by the district transport committee`
    AND p's `within the approved yearly budget`
    AND (NOT p's `can be combined with existing pupil transport`)
    AND (NOT p's `public transport lines can be used`)
    AND (NOT p's `pupils walk the way`)
    AND (NOT (p's `for parents' or staff meetings, home visits and the like` AND p's `the teachers receive the travel allowance`))

-- 4.9 bars a REFUND of expenses on the same terms as organised transport.
GIVEN `for parents' or staff meetings, home visits and the like` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives the travel allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a refund of expenses may be approved under 4.9`
        `for parents' or staff meetings, home visits and the like`
        `receives the travel allowance` IF
    NOT (`for parents' or staff meetings, home visits and the like` AND `receives the travel allowance`)

-- 4.3 also bars the travel ALLOWANCE where pupil transport can carry the
-- teachers.
GIVEN p IS A `transport proposal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the allowance is barred by pupil transport` p IF
    p's `can be combined with existing pupil transport`

-- 4.3, second half: the local authority's vehicle where it is cheaper.
GIVEN `cost in the local authority's vehicle` IS A NUMBER, `cost otherwise` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `use the local authority's vehicle` `cost in the local authority's vehicle` `cost otherwise` IF
    `cost in the local authority's vehicle` LESS THAN `cost otherwise`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `transport action`
DECIDE `the local authority organises` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `organise the transport and set a pick-up point`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 1.9.2.4.2: the local authority the teachers are taken to organises the transport"

-- 4.5: taken from the main road, the public-transport fares to and from it
-- are paid in full.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_5
GIVEN `fare to the main road` IS A NUMBER, `fare from the main road` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `refund for the main-road legs` `fare to the main road` `fare from the main road` IS
    `fare to the main road` PLUS `fare from the main road`

-- 4.6: once a day each way, and the principals build the timetable for it.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_6
`organised journeys a day each way` MEANS 1

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `transport action`
DECIDE `principals build the timetable` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `build the timetable for one pick-up and one drop-off`
    LEST BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.9.2.4.6: the timetable is built so that one pick-up and one drop-off suffice"

-- 4.9 ¶2–4: with a private car, refund at public-transport fares, or at the
-- Accountant-General's car rates (variable costs only) if the Ministry so
-- considers; teachers on organised transport claim duty journeys on the
-- per-diem form, at public-transport fares, up to the comptroller's ceiling.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_9/p2
GIVEN `public-transport fare` IS A NUMBER
      `variable private-car cost at the Accountant-General's rates` IS A NUMBER
      `the Ministry allows the car rates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `refund to a private-car user`
        `public-transport fare`
        `variable private-car cost at the Accountant-General's rates`
        `the Ministry allows the car rates` IS
    IF `the Ministry allows the car rates`
    THEN `variable private-car cost at the Accountant-General's rates`
    ELSE `public-transport fare`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_9/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_9/p4
GIVEN `employed by the Ministry of Education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc "מורים עובדי משרד החינוך"
      `on organised transport and without the allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `fares of the duty journeys` IS A NUMBER
      `the comptroller's ceiling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `duty-journey refund for an organised-transport teacher`
        `employed by the Ministry of Education`
        `on organised transport and without the allowance`
        `fares of the duty journeys`
        `the comptroller's ceiling` IS
    IF `employed by the Ministry of Education` AND `on organised transport and without the allowance`
    THEN min `fares of the duty journeys` `the comptroller's ceiling`
    ELSE 0

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_10
GIVEN `missed the organised transport` IS A BOOLEAN, `fare of the other transport` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `refund for other transport` `missed the organised transport` `fare of the other transport` IS
    IF `missed the organised transport` THEN 0 ELSE `fare of the other transport`

-- 4.11: the employee's request, on the form, reaches the head of the local
-- authority's education department by 15 June (school month 10).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_11
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `transport action`
DECIDE `requesting organised transport` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `submit a request for organised transport`
    WITHIN `month number` June

-- 4.11 ¶2: the head of the education department submits the request for the
-- district committee's approval, as for pupil transport.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_11/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.9 party` `transport action`
DECIDE `the district committee decides the request` IS
    PARTY `the head of the local education department`
    MUST  `pass the request to the district committee`
    HENCE (PARTY `the district transport committee`
           MAY   `approve organised transport`)
    LEST BREACH BY `the head of the local education department` BECAUSE "section 1.9.2.4.11: the head of the education department submits the request for the district committee's approval"

-- 4.12: the cost in a local authority's (yellow) vehicle follows the
-- pupil-transport procedures of the time; an input.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2__para_4__subpara_12
GIVEN `cost by the pupil-transport procedures` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `cost of transport in a local authority's vehicle` `cost by the pupil-transport procedures` IS
    `cost by the pupil-transport procedures`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_2/p1 The subsection's source (אסמכתא): a director-general's circular.

§§ `1.9.3 הוצאות נסיעה בתפקיד`

DECLARE `duty-travel group` IS ONE OF
    `works in an educational institution`
    `role-holder on a global duty-travel rate`
    `in guidance, supervision or curriculum writing`

-- 1: until 31.3.82, from 1.4.79, duty journeys after hours were refunded
-- at public-transport fares under the takshir.
-- 2: from 1.4.82 (the date printed for post-primary), those in institutions
-- get 25% of their travel allowance instead; role-holders found entitled to
-- a global rate, and those in guidance, supervision, curriculum writing and
-- the like, keep the refund the existing instructions give them.
-- 3: from 1.9.90, the duty-travel refund is abolished for teaching employees
-- in whose area of residence the free monthly pass was introduced.
-- F-1.9-d: the clause abolishes the "refund", the name 1.9.3.2 gives the
-- payment it keeps for role-holders and guidance staff, not the
-- "compensation" it pays institution teachers. The reading adopted takes the
-- clause's own subject, every teaching employee in a pass area, and ends
-- whatever duty-travel payment that employee receives.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_3__para_1/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_3__para_1/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_3__para_2/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_3__para_2/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_3__para_2/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_3__para_3/p1
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      g IS A `duty-travel group`
      `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `travel allowance paid` IS A NUMBER
      `public-transport fares of the duty journeys` IS A NUMBER
      `refund under the existing instructions` IS A NUMBER @desc for a role-holder, the global rate he was found entitled to; for guidance, supervision, curriculum writing and the like, the refund the existing instructions give (section 1.9.3.2); an input
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `duty-travel compensation` d g `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives` `travel allowance paid` `public-transport fares of the duty journeys` `refund under the existing instructions` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1979))) THEN 0
           IF (d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1990)) AND `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives`
              THEN 0
           IF (NOT (d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1982)))
              THEN `public-transport fares of the duty journeys`
           IF (NOT (g EQUALS `works in an educational institution`))
              THEN `refund under the existing instructions`
           OTHERWISE 25% TIMES `travel allowance paid`

-- F-1.9-d's evidence: what each paragraph of 1.9.3 calls the payment it
-- makes, and whether institution teachers receive it after 1.4.82.
DECLARE `duty-travel payment` HAS
    `named in`  IS A STRING
    `called`    IS A STRING  @desc "refund" for the text's החזר הוצאות נסיעה בתפקיד, "compensation" for its פיצוי כולל
    `reaches institution teachers after 1.4.82` IS A BOOLEAN

`the duty-travel payments 1.9.3 names` MEANS
    LIST `duty-travel payment` "1.9.3.1"    "refund"       FALSE,
         `duty-travel payment` "1.9.3.2"    "compensation" TRUE,
         `duty-travel payment` "1.9.3.2 p2" "refund"       FALSE

`what 1.9.3.3 abolishes is called` MEANS "refund"

`what 1.9.3.3 abolishes by name no institution teacher receives after 1.4.82` MEANS
    all (GIVEN q YIELD (NOT (q's `called` EQUALS `what 1.9.3.3 abolishes is called`))
                       OR (NOT q's `reaches institution teachers after 1.4.82`))
        `the duty-travel payments 1.9.3 names`
#ASSERT `what 1.9.3.3 abolishes by name no institution teacher receives after 1.4.82`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_3/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_3/p2 The subsection's source (אסמכתא): a director-general's circular.

§§ `1.9.4 הוצאות נסיעה לעובדי הוראה משתלמים`

DECLARE `study framework` IS ONE OF
    `academic studies at a higher-education institution or academic college`
    `retraining or certification at a teacher-training institution`
    `courses and study days initiated by the Ministry's supervision`
    `another framework`

@desc A teaching employee's further studies, as section 1.9.4 asks about them.
DECLARE `further studies` HAS
    `employed by the Ministry or an owner in its tuition-refund arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `framework`                                IS A `study framework`
    `on a full or partial sabbatical`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `inter-city fares`                         IS A NUMBER
    `urban fares`                              IS A NUMBER
    `form approved by the direct manager`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `confirmation of studies attached`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a study-hours grant or tuition refund` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `study-travel action` IS ONE OF
    `attach the request to the attendance report`
    `pay the month's part of the refund`
    `send the half-yearly summary`
    `transfer the refunds to the owner`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_1__para_1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_1__para_2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_1__para_3
GIVEN s IS A `further studies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to study-travel refund` s IF
        s's `employed by the Ministry or an owner in its tuition-refund arrangements`
    AND (NOT (s's `framework` EQUALS `another framework`))
    AND (NOT s's `on a full or partial sabbatical`)

-- 1: the request is on a form the direct manager approves, with a
-- confirmation of studies unless a study-hours grant or tuition refund was
-- approved.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_2__para_1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_2__para_1/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_2__para_1/p3
GIVEN s IS A `further studies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the request is complete` s IF
        s's `form approved by the direct manager`
    AND (s's `confirmation of studies attached` OR s's `has a study-hours grant or tuition refund`)

-- 4 (eligibility): only inter-city journeys; urban fares are not refunded.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_1__para_4
GIVEN s IS A `further studies`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `fares refunded for studies` s IS
    s's `inter-city fares`

-- Procedures 2–3: one request for all the planned journeys of the studies;
-- for a supervision course, guidance day or study day, one a month.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_2__para_2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_2__para_3
GIVEN f IS A `study framework`
      `months the studies run` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `requests the studies take` f `months the studies run` IS
    IF f EQUALS `courses and study days initiated by the Ministry's supervision`
    THEN `months the studies run`
    ELSE 1

-- 4: the signed request goes with the monthly attendance report.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_2__para_4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `study-travel action`
DECIDE `the request travels with the attendance report` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `attach the request to the attendance report`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.9.4: the signed request is attached to the monthly attendance report"

§§§ `1.9.4 The refund, as its paragraphs compose`

@export The travel refund for further studies a teaching employee is owed under section 1.9.4 of the takanon
GIVEN s IS A `further studies` @desc the employee's studies
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `study-travel refund` s IS
    IF `entitled to study-travel refund` s AND `the request is complete` s
    THEN `fares refunded for studies` s
    ELSE 0

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4__hc_2__para_5 Where the forms can be had (district offices, training centres, school offices); no rule.

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4/p1 A heading: "התשלום".

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `study-travel action`
DECIDE `the employer's treasury pays monthly` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the month's part of the refund`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 1.9.4: the employer's treasury pays the month's part of the refund each month"

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4/p3 A heading: "התחשבנויות עם הבעלויות".

-- Owners send a half-yearly summary (6 months), then the Ministry transfers.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4/p4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `study-travel action`
DECIDE `owners' half-yearly accounting` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `send the half-yearly summary`
    WITHIN 6
    HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
           MUST  `transfer the refunds to the owner`
           LEST BREACH BY `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "section 1.9.4: the Ministry transfers the approved refunds to the owners")
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 1.9.4: owners send a half-yearly summary of refunds"

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_9__ssec_1_9_4/p6 The title of the request form and the line introducing it; the form is not a rule.

-- Worked examples. Every amount below is a placeholder.
`a pass user on unpaid leave` MEANS
    `commuting month` WITH
        `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives` IS TRUE
        `passes the journey needs`                IS 2
        `price of a monthly pass`                 IS 200
        `days employed a week`                    IS 5
        `real travel expenses of the month`       IS 0
        `needs transport to reach work`           IS TRUE
        `published allowance for a full month`    IS 0
        `published allowance per journey`         IS 0
        `required to attend only some days`       IS FALSE
        `journeys made`                           IS 0
        `in a month after the first of a continuous paid absence longer than a month` IS FALSE
        `in a month after the first of reserve duty longer than a month` IS FALSE
        `on unpaid leave`                         IS TRUE
        `work temporarily stopped`                IS FALSE
        `a month of the summer break`             IS FALSE

#ASSERT `commuting allowance` `a pass user on unpaid leave` EQUALS 0

-- 1א ¶4 "בכל מקרה": two days a week, attending on those days only, is paid
-- real expenses (90), not 8 journeys at the published allowance (48).
`a two-day pass user who attends on those days only` MEANS
    `commuting month` WITH
        `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives` IS TRUE
        `passes the journey needs`                IS 1
        `price of a monthly pass`                 IS 200
        `days employed a week`                    IS 2
        `real travel expenses of the month`       IS 90
        `needs transport to reach work`           IS TRUE
        `published allowance for a full month`    IS 250
        `published allowance per journey`         IS 6
        `required to attend only some days`       IS TRUE
        `journeys made`                           IS 8
        `in a month after the first of a continuous paid absence longer than a month` IS FALSE
        `in a month after the first of reserve duty longer than a month` IS FALSE
        `on unpaid leave`                         IS FALSE
        `work temporarily stopped`                IS FALSE
        `a month of the summer break`             IS FALSE

#ASSERT `commuting allowance` `a two-day pass user who attends on those days only` EQUALS 90
#ASSERT `allowance where a pass operates` `a pass user on unpaid leave` EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `may claim for the second bus` 2 3 FALSE
#ASSERT `duty-travel compensation` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1985) `works in an educational institution` FALSE 400 90 0 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `duty-travel compensation` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1995) `works in an educational institution` TRUE 400 90 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `duty-travel compensation` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1995) `in guidance, supervision or curriculum writing` FALSE 400 90 150 EQUALS 150

-- F-1.9-c's evidence: a teacher who meets 2ב and 2ד alike.
`a teacher who moved away and was not placed` MEANS
    `work outside the jurisdiction` WITH
        `posted there for the system's needs`           IS FALSE
        `moved home out of the jurisdiction`            IS TRUE
        `the move raised the travel expenses or first made them payable` IS TRUE
        `moved at the Ministry's demand`                IS FALSE
        `moved for personal reasons the committee recognised` IS FALSE
        `in official education`                         IS TRUE
        `asked for a transfer and the Ministry agreed`  IS FALSE
        `the transfer took the workplace further from home` IS FALSE
        `moved to another city and still works in the old one` IS TRUE
        `asked for work in the new city and was not placed for two years` IS TRUE
        `a realistic placement in the new city was not used` IS TRUE
        `real bus fares for the days travelled`         IS 0
        `allowance before the move`                     IS 0
        `allowance at the previous workplace`           IS 0
        `allowance on the present journey`              IS 300

`2ב and 2ד both reach a teacher who moved away and was not placed` MEANS
        `frozen at the rate before the move under 2ב` `a teacher who moved away and was not placed`
    AND `paid travel expenses under 2ד` `a teacher who moved away and was not placed`
    AND NOT (`a teacher who moved away and was not placed`'s `allowance before the move`
             EQUALS `a teacher who moved away and was not placed`'s `allowance on the present journey`)
#ASSERT `2ב and 2ד both reach a teacher who moved away and was not placed`
#ASSERT `allowance outside the jurisdiction` `a teacher who moved away and was not placed` EQUALS 300

#TRACE `requesting organised transport` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `submit a request for organised transport` AT 9
#TRACE `the district committee decides the request` AT 9 WITH
    PARTY `the head of the local education department` DOES `pass the request to the district committee` AT 10
#TRACE `owners' half-yearly accounting` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `send the half-yearly summary` AT 6

§§ `Property checks`

-- The section's rules over their whole finite space: every combination of
-- a commuting month's flags with 1 to 6 days a week, one to three passes and
-- each of the five bars; every journey of one to three buses and 0 to 6
-- stops; every spread of 6 to 24 hours over one to three schools; every
-- combination of the eleven conditions of 1.9.1.2; every group of 1.9.3 on
-- each boundary day the text names and the day before it; and every
-- framework of 1.9.4 with each of its flags.

-- A commuting month built from the flags under test. Amounts are
-- placeholders: a pass of 200, real expenses of 90, a published 250 a month
-- or 6 a journey, 8 journeys made. `bar` 0 is no bar; 1 to 5 set one of
-- the five bars of 1ב.5 and 1ב.6.
GIVEN pass IS A BOOLEAN, days IS A NUMBER, some IS A BOOLEAN, needs IS A BOOLEAN
      passes IS A NUMBER, bar IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `commuting month`
DECIDE `a checked month` pass days some needs passes bar IS
    `commuting month` WITH
        `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives` IS pass
        `passes the journey needs`                IS passes
        `price of a monthly pass`                 IS 200
        `days employed a week`                    IS days
        `real travel expenses of the month`       IS 90
        `needs transport to reach work`           IS needs
        `published allowance for a full month`    IS 250
        `published allowance per journey`         IS 6
        `required to attend only some days`       IS some
        `journeys made`                           IS 8
        `in a month after the first of a continuous paid absence longer than a month` IS bar EQUALS 1
        `in a month after the first of reserve duty longer than a month` IS bar EQUALS 2
        `on unpaid leave`                         IS bar EQUALS 3
        `work temporarily stopped`                IS bar EQUALS 4
        `a month of the summer break`             IS bar EQUALS 5

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE

GIVEN pass IS A BOOLEAN, days IS A NUMBER, some IS A BOOLEAN, needs IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `commuting month`
DECIDE `the checked months for` pass days some needs IS
    concat (map (GIVEN passes YIELD map (GIVEN bar YIELD `a checked month` pass days some needs passes bar) (range 0 5))
                (LIST 1, 2, 3))

`every checked month` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN pass YIELD
                    concat (map (GIVEN days YIELD
                                    concat (map (GIVEN some YIELD
                                                    concat (map (GIVEN needs YIELD `the checked months for` pass days some needs)
                                                                `both booleans`))
                                                `both booleans`))
                                (range 1 6)))
                `both booleans`)

#ASSERT count `every checked month` EQUALS 864

-- 1ב.5–6 (and, through 1א's note, for pass users too): a barred month pays
-- nothing, whoever the employee is; every other month pays a non-negative
-- amount.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN m YIELD
                    `commuting allowance` m AT LEAST 0
                AND ((NOT `no allowance this month` m) OR `commuting allowance` m EQUALS 0))
            `every checked month`

-- 1א ¶4, "בכל מקרה": every pass user employed one or two days a week in a
-- month no bar reaches is paid her real expenses, whatever else holds.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN m YIELD
                    (NOT m's `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives`)
                 OR `no allowance this month` m
                 OR m's `days employed a week` GREATER THAN 2
                 OR `commuting allowance` m EQUALS m's `real travel expenses of the month`)
            `every checked month`

-- 1א ¶2–3: a pass user who attends every day is refunded at most two
-- passes, however many the journey needs.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN m YIELD
                    `allowance where a pass operates` m
                    AT MOST 2 TIMES m's `price of a monthly pass`
                 OR `paid real expenses in any case` m)
            `every checked month`

-- 1ב.1: where no pass operates, one who needs no transport is paid nothing.
-- 1א names no such condition, and its note brings in 1ב.3, 1ב.5 and 1ב.6
-- but not 1ב.1 (F-1.9-e): where a pass operates, a teacher employed three
-- days or more who needs no transport to reach work is paid the price of a
-- pass. The two regimes part on exactly that teacher.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN m YIELD
                    m's `needs transport to reach work`
                 OR m's `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives`
                 OR `commuting allowance` m EQUALS 0)
            `every checked month`

GIVEN m IS A `commuting month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid where she needs no transport` m IF
        (NOT m's `needs transport to reach work`)
    AND `commuting allowance` m GREATER THAN 0

`the months that pay one who needs no transport` MEANS
    filter `paid where she needs no transport` `every checked month`

#ASSERT all (GIVEN m YIELD
                    m's `a free monthly pass operates where the employee lives`
                AND (NOT `no allowance this month` m))
            `the months that pay one who needs no transport`

`a pass area pays a teacher who needs no transport to reach work` MEANS
        `paid where she needs no transport` (`a checked month` TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE 1 0)
    AND `commuting allowance` (`a checked month` TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE 1 0) EQUALS 200
    AND `commuting allowance` (`a checked month` FALSE 5 FALSE FALSE 1 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `a pass area pays a teacher who needs no transport to reach work`

-- 1ב.2 over one to three buses, 0 to 6 urban stops and either way of
-- walking: the second bus is claimed only with two buses or more, 3 stops
-- or more and no shorter walk; and one more stop never takes the claim away.
GIVEN buses IS A NUMBER, walk IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the second-bus rule holds for` buses walk IF
        all (GIVEN stops YIELD
                `may claim for the second bus` buses stops walk
                EQUALS (buses AT LEAST 2 AND stops AT LEAST 3 AND NOT walk))
            (range 0 6)
    AND and (zipWith (GIVEN s, t YIELD
                        (NOT `may claim for the second bus` buses s walk)
                        OR `may claim for the second bus` buses t walk)
                     (range 0 6) (drop 1 (range 0 6)))

#ASSERT all (GIVEN buses YIELD all (GIVEN walk YIELD `the second-bus rule holds for` buses walk) `both booleans`)
            (LIST 1, 2, 3)

-- 1ב.4 over every spread of 6, 12, 18 or 24 hours over one to three
-- schools: the allowance always attaches to some school, only to one with
-- the greatest hours, and to more than one exactly where the greatest is
-- shared (F-1.9-b over the whole space).
`the hours a school may hold` MEANS LIST 6, 12, 18, 24

`every spread over one to three schools` MEANS
    append (map (GIVEN a YIELD LIST a) `the hours a school may hold`)
           (append (concat (map (GIVEN a YIELD map (GIVEN b YIELD LIST a, b) `the hours a school may hold`)
                                `the hours a school may hold`))
                   (concat (map (GIVEN a YIELD
                                    concat (map (GIVEN b YIELD map (GIVEN c YIELD LIST a, b, c) `the hours a school may hold`)
                                                `the hours a school may hold`))
                                `the hours a school may hold`)))

#ASSERT count `every spread over one to three schools` EQUALS 84
#ASSERT all (GIVEN hs YIELD
                    count (`schools the allowance attaches to` hs) AT LEAST 1
                AND all (GIVEN h YIELD h EQUALS maximum hs) (`schools the allowance attaches to` hs)
                AND (count (`schools the allowance attaches to` hs) GREATER THAN 1)
                    EQUALS (count (filter (GIVEN h YIELD h EQUALS maximum hs) hs) GREATER THAN 1))
            `every spread over one to three schools`

-- 1.9.1.2 over every combination of its eleven conditions. The amounts are
-- placeholders chosen to tell the clauses apart: real bus fares 100, the
-- rate before the move 200, at the previous workplace 250, the present
-- journey 300.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF (LIST OF BOOLEAN)
DECIDE `every row of booleans of length` n IS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN LIST EMPTY
    ELSE concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD LIST (TRUE FOLLOWED BY r), (FALSE FOLLOWED BY r))
                     (`every row of booleans of length` (n MINUS 1)))

GIVEN r IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `work outside the jurisdiction`
DECIDE `the teacher of row` r IS
    `work outside the jurisdiction` WITH
        `posted there for the system's needs`           IS at r 0
        `moved home out of the jurisdiction`            IS at r 1
        `the move raised the travel expenses or first made them payable` IS at r 2
        `moved at the Ministry's demand`                IS at r 3
        `moved for personal reasons the committee recognised` IS at r 4
        `in official education`                         IS at r 5
        `asked for a transfer and the Ministry agreed`  IS at r 6
        `the transfer took the workplace further from home` IS at r 7
        `moved to another city and still works in the old one` IS at r 8
        `asked for work in the new city and was not placed for two years` IS at r 9
        `a realistic placement in the new city was not used` IS at r 10
        `real bus fares for the days travelled`         IS 100
        `allowance before the move`                     IS 200
        `allowance at the previous workplace`           IS 250
        `allowance on the present journey`              IS 300

-- A teacher posted for the system's needs neither asked for her transfer
-- (2ג) nor chose to keep working in the city she left (2ד); those rows are
-- left out as cases the words exclude.
`every teacher outside the jurisdiction` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN w YIELD
                (NOT w's `posted there for the system's needs`)
             OR ((NOT w's `asked for a transfer and the Ministry agreed`)
                 AND (NOT w's `moved to another city and still works in the old one`)))
           (map `the teacher of row` (`every row of booleans of length` 11))

DECLARE `clause of 1.9.1.2` IS ONE OF `2א`, `2ב`, `2ג`, `2ד`

GIVEN w IS A `work outside the jurisdiction`
GIVETH A LIST OF `clause of 1.9.1.2`
DECIDE `the clauses that reach` w IS
    concat (LIST (IF `paid real bus fares as posted` w THEN LIST `2א` ELSE EMPTY)
               , (IF `frozen at the rate before the move under 2ב` w THEN LIST `2ב` ELSE EMPTY)
               , (IF `held at the previous workplace's rate under 2ג` w THEN LIST `2ג` ELSE EMPTY)
               , (IF `paid travel expenses under 2ד` w THEN LIST `2ד` ELSE EMPTY))

GIVEN c IS A `clause of 1.9.1.2`, w IS A `work outside the jurisdiction`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what clause` c `pays` w IS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `2א` THEN w's `real bus fares for the days travelled`
    WHEN `2ב` THEN min (w's `allowance on the present journey`) (w's `allowance before the move`)
    WHEN `2ג` THEN min (w's `allowance on the present journey`) (w's `allowance at the previous workplace`)
    WHEN `2ד` THEN w's `allowance on the present journey`

-- Consistency: wherever one clause reaches the teacher, the allowance is
-- that clause's; wherever none does, it is the present journey's.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN w YIELD
                CONSIDER `the clauses that reach` w
                WHEN EMPTY THEN `allowance outside the jurisdiction` w EQUALS w's `allowance on the present journey`
                WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
                    (NOT (rest EQUALS EMPTY))
                    OR `allowance outside the jurisdiction` w EQUALS `what clause` c `pays` w)
            `every teacher outside the jurisdiction`

-- Overlap (F-1.9-f): the pairs of 2א–2ד that reach one teacher and pay her
-- different amounts. 2ב with 2ד is F-1.9-c; the text orders none of the
-- others either.
GIVEN a IS A `clause of 1.9.1.2`, b IS A `clause of 1.9.1.2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `clauses` a `and` b `part on some teacher` IF
    any (GIVEN w YIELD
                elem a (`the clauses that reach` w)
            AND elem b (`the clauses that reach` w)
            AND NOT (`what clause` a `pays` w EQUALS `what clause` b `pays` w))
        `every teacher outside the jurisdiction`

`2א, 2ב, 2ג and 2ד reach one teacher with different rates and set no order` MEANS
        `clauses` `2א` `and` `2ב` `part on some teacher`
    AND `clauses` `2ב` `and` `2ג` `part on some teacher`
    AND `clauses` `2ג` `and` `2ד` `part on some teacher`
#ASSERT `2א, 2ב, 2ג and 2ד reach one teacher with different rates and set no order`
#ASSERT `clauses` `2ב` `and` `2ד` `part on some teacher`
#ASSERT NOT `clauses` `2א` `and` `2ג` `part on some teacher`
#ASSERT NOT `clauses` `2א` `and` `2ד` `part on some teacher`

-- 1.9.3 over every group, both kinds of area, and each boundary day the
-- text names (1.4.79, 1.4.82, 1.9.90) with the day before it. Fares 90, a
-- travel allowance of 400 and a refund under the existing instructions of
-- 150 are placeholders.
`the duty-travel days checked` MEANS
    LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 1979, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1979
       , DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 1982, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1982
       , DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 1990, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1990, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024

`every duty-travel group` MEANS
    LIST `works in an educational institution`, `role-holder on a global duty-travel rate`
       , `in guidance, supervision or curriculum writing`

GIVEN d IS A DATE, g IS A `duty-travel group`, pass IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `duty travel checked on` d g pass IS
    `duty-travel compensation` d g pass 400 90 150

-- Never negative, and never more than the larger of the three measures.
-- From 1.4.79 to 31.3.82 every group is refunded the fares (clause 1);
-- from 1.4.82 an institution teacher gets 25% of the allowance and the
-- others their existing refund (clause 2); from 1.9.90 nobody in a pass
-- area is paid (clause 3, read as F-1.9-d reads it), and outside one
-- clause 2 goes on.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD
                all (GIVEN g YIELD
                        all (GIVEN pass YIELD
                                    `duty travel checked on` d g pass AT LEAST 0
                                AND `duty travel checked on` d g pass AT MOST 150)
                            `both booleans`)
                    `every duty-travel group`)
            `the duty-travel days checked`

#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD
                all (GIVEN pass YIELD
                            `duty travel checked on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1979) g pass EQUALS 90
                        AND `duty travel checked on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 1982) g pass EQUALS 90
                        AND `duty travel checked on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1982) g pass
                            EQUALS (IF g EQUALS `works in an educational institution` THEN 100 ELSE 150)
                        AND `duty travel checked on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 1990) g pass
                            EQUALS `duty travel checked on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1982) g pass
                        AND `duty travel checked on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1990) g pass
                            EQUALS (IF pass THEN 0 ELSE `duty travel checked on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1982) g pass))
                    `both booleans`)
            `every duty-travel group`

-- 1.9.4 over every framework and each of its six flags: the refund is never
-- negative, never more than the inter-city fares, never touched by the
-- urban fares, and nothing outside the three frameworks or on a sabbatical.
GIVEN f IS A `study framework`, urban IS A NUMBER, r IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `further studies`
DECIDE `the studies of` f `with urban fares` urban `and row` r IS
    `further studies` WITH
        `employed by the Ministry or an owner in its tuition-refund arrangements` IS at r 0
        `framework`                                IS f
        `on a full or partial sabbatical`          IS at r 1
        `inter-city fares`                         IS 120
        `urban fares`                              IS urban
        `form approved by the direct manager`      IS at r 2
        `confirmation of studies attached`         IS at r 3
        `has a study-hours grant or tuition refund` IS at r 4

`every study framework` MEANS
    LIST `academic studies at a higher-education institution or academic college`
       , `retraining or certification at a teacher-training institution`
       , `courses and study days initiated by the Ministry's supervision`
       , `another framework`

#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD
                all (GIVEN r YIELD
                            `study-travel refund` (`the studies of` f `with urban fares` 0 `and row` r) AT LEAST 0
                        AND `study-travel refund` (`the studies of` f `with urban fares` 0 `and row` r) AT MOST 120
                        AND `study-travel refund` (`the studies of` f `with urban fares` 0 `and row` r)
                            EQUALS `study-travel refund` (`the studies of` f `with urban fares` 50 `and row` r)
                        AND ((NOT (f EQUALS `another framework` OR at r 1))
                             OR `study-travel refund` (`the studies of` f `with urban fares` 0 `and row` r) EQUALS 0))
                    (`every row of booleans of length` 5))
            `every study framework`

-- Procedures 2–3: every framework files at least one request, and one a
-- month at most, over studies of 1 to 12 months.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD
                all (GIVEN months YIELD
                            `requests the studies take` f months AT LEAST 1
                        AND `requests the studies take` f months AT MOST months)
                    (range 1 12))
            `every study framework`
